      "kind": "lede",
      "html": "<p>Uncontrolled energy in maintenance is one of the worst risks in a factory. A machine starts with a hand in it. A line is not vented. A capacitor still holds charge. A LOTO audit checks that safe isolation was really done. Write the record at the isolator, not after the job.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>Safe isolation is part of the safe system of work under the Health and Safety at Work etc Act 1974 and PUWER 1998.</li><li>The steps: identify every energy source, isolate, lock and tag, then prove zero energy.</li><li>Energy is not only electrical. It includes air, hydraulic, heat, gravity, springs and capacitors.</li><li>Higher-risk maintenance usually sits inside a permit to work. The audit checks both.</li><li>The lock and the proof of zero energy keep people safe. The audit records that they were done.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The law",
      "heading": "Where LOTO fits in UK law",
      "html": "<p>Great Britain has no single lockout tagout regulation. Safe isolation is part of the safe system of work under the Health and Safety at Work etc Act 1974. PUWER 1998 requires work equipment to be safe during maintenance. Electrical work brings in the Electricity at Work Regulations 1989.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The steps",
      "heading": "What a safe isolation audit covers",
      "html": "<p>Find every energy source. Shut down and isolate at the right point. Put on a lock and a personal danger tag. Where several people work, each adds a lock. Release or hold back stored energy. Prove zero energy before work starts.</p><p>Each machine and site has its own procedure. Treat this as a start, not the whole procedure.</p>"
    },
